@startuml FIG-CL-TAV-06
skinparam shadowing false
title FIG-CL-TAV-06 Diagnostic sequence\nSysML 1.6 notation-based views; executable/metamodel conformance is not claimed\nfailure, overlapping observation, preparatory action, later distinguishing test

actor Operator
participant "Msess" as S
participant "Mprot" as P
participant "Analysis / Diagnosis" as A

Operator -> S : start session, H0 = {h_normal} union H_single
S -> S : Select ta (worst remaining 2; overlap possible)
S -> P : Execute ta
P --> S : observation class a (keeps h1 and h2)
S -> A : Izk
A --> S : Hk = {h1, h2}; overlapping observation, not proved equivalent
S -> S : no currently usable distinguisher at qk
S -> P : Prep action (changes observable q)
P --> S : qk+1
S -> S : Select later distinguishing test tb
S -> P : Execute tb
P --> S : observation that splits h1 / h2
A --> S : Hk singleton or still indistinguishable
note over S, A
  Prep is a session step. It must spend the same
  cmin / B or Kmax resource as an ordinary test.
end note
@enduml
